# SonarCloud — agent debug playbook

> Status: `sonarqube.yml` + `sonar-project.properties` are in the repo, but Sonar goes live only after the SonarCloud project + `SONAR_TOKEN`/`SONAR_HOST_URL` secrets are set. The `sonar:report` / `sonar-fetch-report.ts` convenience tooling and the `sonar-report` artifact are ported when that tooling is wired — until then read the SonarCloud dashboard + CI logs.

## CI logs (GitHub Actions)

```bash
gh run list --workflow=sonarqube.yml --limit 5
gh run view <run-id> --log-failed
```

## Report artifact / local API

Every SonarQube run uploads `sonar-report.md`:

```bash
gh run list --workflow=sonarqube.yml --limit 1
gh run download <run-id> -n sonar-report   # read sonar-report/sonar-report.md
```

Local report needs a token (never commit): `.env` with `SONAR_TOKEN` (+ optional `SONAR_HOST_URL=https://sonarcloud.io`), then `npm run sonar:report`. Project keys come from `sonar-project.properties` (`sonar.organization=sanchahous`, `sonar.projectKey=sanchahous_ai-today-brief`).

## One-time setup

If the scan fails with *"CI analysis while Automatic Analysis is enabled"*: SonarCloud → Project Settings → Administration → **Analysis Method** → disable **Automatic Analysis** (keep CI-based analysis only). Without this, `sonarqube.yml` exits non-zero even when checks pass.

## Free plan

- Only the **Sonar way** gate (custom gates need a paid plan). **New Code** is measured vs `main` (`sonar.newCode.referenceBranch=main`).
- `sonar.qualitygate.wait=false` → a red gate on the site does **not** fail CI. Read the report, not just the letter grade. Fix **new-code** issues, not legacy.

## "Not working" checklist

1. Automatic Analysis = **OFF** (required for CI). 2. GitHub Secrets `SONAR_TOKEN` + `SONAR_HOST_URL`. 3. Red gate at the start is normal. 4. Re-run: Actions → SonarQube → Run workflow (`workflow_dispatch`). 5. Local: `npm run sonar:report` (needs `.env` `SONAR_TOKEN`).
